# Installed agent skills (`npx skills add`) — regenerable from skills-lock.json.
# The lock file stays tracked; the bulky skill payloads and their Claude Code
# symlinks do not (mirrors package-lock.json vs node_modules).
#
# `.claude/skills/` is MIXED: 25 of its 34 entries are symlinks into `.agents/skills/`
# carrying absolute machine paths (`/e/AI_Development/...`) — worthless in git and broken
# on any other clone. The rest are hand-authored PRODUCT skills that ship to customers via
# the kit (CLAUDE_SKILLS_ALLOWLIST in scripts/sync-to-orchestrator.mjs) and do deserve
# version history.
#
# So this is `/*` + explicit opt-in rather than a blanket directory ignore: a directory
# excluded with a trailing slash is never descended into, and a negation for anything
# beneath it cannot re-include it. Ignoring the entries individually keeps negation working.
# Default is still "not tracked" — add a line below only for a skill that is genuinely
# product, never for an installed one.
.agents/
.claude/skills/*
!.claude/skills/wxUIUXCodeReview/
!.claude/skills/wxBrand/
!.claude/skills/wxG-O-D/
!.claude/skills/wxBrainstorm/
# SCOPE-138: wxHelpGenerate is shipped (CLAUDE_SKILLS_ALLOWLIST); without this line its new
# files (scripts/teach.mjs) were ignored while the force-added older ones stayed tracked.
!.claude/skills/wxHelpGenerate/
# Repo-authored dev tooling (not shipped: absent from CLAUDE_SKILLS_ALLOWLIST) — /run-wxkanban
!.claude/skills/run-wxkanban/

# wxKanban kit — cached signed entitlement token (per-developer; never commit)
.wxai/.entitlement

# Help-staleness marker written by .husky/pre-push and cleared by /wxRefreshHelp.
# Per-developer to-do; tracking it would conflict on nearly every push.
.wxai/help-stale.json

